  "issue": {
    "id": "I_kwDOAd1its7bthV8",
    "databaseId": 3686143356,
    "number": 1770,
    "title": "Core ROS 2 package has `ros-kilted-rmw-zenoh-cpp` as direct dependency",
    "url": "https://github.com/ros2/ros2/issues/1770",
    "body": "### Generated by Generative AI\n\nNo\n\n### Operating System:\n\nLinux Ubuntu 24.04\n\n### ROS version or commit hash:\n\n`kilted`, probably `rolling` too\n\n### RMW implementation (if applicable):\n\n_No response_\n\n### RMW Configuration (if applicable):\n\n_No response_\n\n### Client library (if applicable):\n\n_No response_\n\n### 'ros2 doctor --report' output\n\n_No response_\n\n### Steps to reproduce issue\n\nTo reproduce just execute:\n`apt remove ros-kilted-rmw-zenoh-cpp`\n\nThis was tested on the latest docker `ros:kilted` image as of 2025.12.02.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nOptional packages like `ros-kilted-rmw-zenoh-cpp` should not be direct dependencies of core ROS 2 packages\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nTrying to remove `ros-kilted-rmw-zenoh-cpp` package through `apt` results in removing core packages of ROS 2 like:\n```\nThe following packages will be REMOVED:\n  ros-kilted-ament-cmake-ros ros-kilted-launch-testing-ros ros-kilted-rmw-test-fixture-implementation\n  ros-kilted-rmw-zenoh-cpp ros-kilted-ros-base ros-kilted-ros-core\n```\n\nReverse dependencies are listed below:\n```\n$ apt rdepends ros-kilted-rmw-zenoh-cpp\nros-kilted-rmw-zenoh-cpp\nReverse Depends:\n  Depends: ros-kilted-rmw-test-fixture-implementation\n$ apt rdepends ros-kilted-rmw-test-fixture-implementation\nros-kilted-rmw-test-fixture-implementation\nReverse Depends:\n  Depends: ros-kilted-ament-cmake-ros\n  Depends: ros-kilted-launch-testing-ros\n$ apt rdepends ros-kilted-ament-cmake-ros\nros-kilted-ament-cmake-ros\nReverse Depends:\n  Depends: ros-kilted-ros-core\n```\n\n\n### Additional information\n\n_No response_",
